"label":"Ch. 27","title":"WAITING"},{"id":"s28","label":"Ch. 28","title":"BLACK SUNDAY"},{"id":"s29","label":"Ch. 29","title":"\"WOUNDED AND MISSING\""},{"id":"s30","label":"Ch. 30","title":"THE TURNING OF THE TIDE"},{"id":"s31","label":"Ch. 31","title":"MRS. MATILDA PITTMAN"},{"id":"s32","label":"Ch. 32","title":"WORD FROM JEM"},{"id":"s33","label":"Ch. 33"},{"id":"s34","label":"Ch. 34","title":"MR. HYDE GOES TO HIS OWN PLACE AND SUSAN TAKES A HONEYMOON"},{"id":"s35","label":"Ch. 35","title":"\"RILLA-MY-RILLA!\""}],"groups":[{"id":"g-pryor","label":"Pryor (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"rilla-blythe","name":"Rilla Blythe","aliases":["Rilla"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Marshall Elliott--were chatting together near the open door that led to the veranda, through which a cool, delicious breeze was blowing, bringing whiffs of phantom perfume from the garden, and charming gay echoes from…”"},{"id":"susan","name":"Susan","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “In the big living-room at Ingleside Susan Baker sat down with a certain grim satisfaction hovering about her like an aura; it was four o'clock and Susan, who had been working incessantly since six that morning, felt t…”"},{"id":"walter-blythe","name":"Walter Blythe","aliases":["Walter"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Marshall Elliott--were chatting together near the open door that led to the veranda, through which a cool, delicious breeze was blowing, bringing whiffs of phantom perfume from the garden, and charming gay echoes from…”"},{"id":"jem","name":"Jem","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"Bruce adores Jem,\" said Mrs Blythe.”"},{"id":"jims","name":"Jims","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “The Ingleside family promptly shortened it to Jims, but Susan obstinately called him \"Little Kitchener\" and nothing else.”"},{"id":"miss-oliver","name":"Miss Oliver","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Marshall Elliott--were chatting together near the open door that led to the veranda, through which a cool, delicious breeze was blowing, bringing whiffs of phantom perfume from the garden, and charming gay echoes from…”"},{"id":"irene-howard","name":"Irene Howard","aliases":["Irene"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “Irene Howard fastened it up for her and gave her some over-sweet, condescending compliments.”"},{"id":"mary-vance","name":"Mary Vance","aliases":["Mary"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Mary ever did or could bloom, with peonies crimson, peonies silvery pink, peonies white as drifts of winter snow.”"},{"id":"upper-glen","name":"Upper Glen","aliases":["Glen"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Therefore Susan had all the comfortable consciousness of a well-dressed woman as she opened her copy of the Daily Enterprise and prepared to read the Glen \"Notes\" which, as Miss Cornelia had just informed her, filled…”"},{"id":"mrs-blythe","name":"Mrs. Blythe","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Mrs.”"},{"id":"miranda-pryor","name":"Miranda Pryor","aliases":["Miranda"],"role":"supporting","group":"g-pryor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Carl Meredith was walking with Miranda Pryor, more to torment Joe Milgrave than for any other reason.”"},{"id":"gertrude","name":"Gertrude","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"I'm so glad Gertrude is going to stay,\" said Mrs.”"},{"id":"cousin-sophia","name":"Cousin Sophia","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “She was so pretty and young and glowing that even Cousin Sophia Crawford was compelled to admire her--and Cousin Sophia Crawford admired few transient earthly things.”"},{"id":"whiskers","name":"Whiskers","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"The church got on very well before old Whiskers-on-the-moon came to the Glen and it is my opinion it will get on without him after he is gone,\" said Susan.”"},{"id":"nan","name":"Nan","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Are Di and Nan going too?\"”"},{"id":"kenneth-ford","name":"Kenneth Ford","aliases":["Kenneth"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Kenneth did--but he stayed with his mother's people over-harbour.”"},{"id":"ken","name":"Ken","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “I saw how you slipped over to the sands with Ken and stayed there ever so long with him.”"},{"id":"shirley-blythe","name":"Shirley Blythe","aliases":["Shirley"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"'Carl Meredith and Shirley Blythe came home last Friday evening from Queen's Academy.”"},{"id":"joe-milgrave","name":"Joe Milgrave","aliases":["Joe"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Carl Meredith was walking with Miranda Pryor, more to torment Joe Milgrave than for any other reason.”"},{"id":"mr-pryor","name":"Mr. Pryor","aliases":["Pryor"],"role":"minor","group":"g-pryor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"Speaking of that reminds me that Mr.”"},{"id":"di","name":"Di","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “She was so nearly fifteen that she called herself that, and she was quite as tall as Di and Nan; also, she was nearly as pretty as Susan believed her to be.”"},{"id":"jerry-meredith","name":"Jerry Meredith","aliases":["Jerry"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “I suppose,\" continued Miss Cornelia, with a side glance at Susan, \"that after the snub I got a few minutes ago it will not be safe for me to suggest that Jerry Meredith is making sheep's eyes at Nan.\"”"},{"id":"germans","name":"Germans","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “It didn't happen often that they had a chance for a talk together; Mary was determined that this one shouldn't be spoiled by Walter Blythe's silly blather about Pipers and Germans and such like absurd things.”"},{"id":"sophia","name":"Sophia","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Albert Crawford.' Why that is my own cousin Sophia, Mrs.”"},{"id":"carl-meredith","name":"Carl Meredith","aliases":["Carl"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"'Carl Meredith and Shirley Blythe came home last Friday evening from Queen's Academy.”"},{"id":"mr-meredith","name":"Mr. Meredith","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"He is through with Queen's now and Mr.”"},{"id":"miller-douglas","name":"Miller Douglas","aliases":["Miller"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “\"'Miller Douglas has decided not to go West.”"},{"id":"kaiser","name":"Kaiser","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “When two people foregathered in those days they talked of the war; and old Highland Sandy of the Harbour Head talked of it when he was alone and hurled anathemas at the Kaiser across all the acres of his farm.”"},{"id":"miss-cornelia","name":"Miss Cornelia","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Therefore Susan had all the comfortable consciousness of a well-dressed woman as she opened her copy of the Daily Enterprise and prepared to read the Glen \"Notes\" which, as Miss Cornelia had just informed her, filled…”"},{"id":"mr-hyde","name":"Mr. Hyde","aliases":["Hyde"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Jekyll had not been Mr.”"},{"id":"fred-arnold","name":"Fred Arnold","aliases":["Fred","Mr. Arnold"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “\"Fred Arnold was at the manse and walked home with me.”"},{"id":"una","name":"Una","ro